    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Apartment 34 Merchamp is a well-positioned one-bedroom first-floor apartment extending to approximately 34.5 sq. m., located within this mature residential development just off Vernon Avenue in Clontarf.\r\n\r\nThe apartment offers bright, well-proportioned accommodation with a practical layout that makes good use of the available space. It will appeal to first-time buyers, those looking to downsize, or purchasers seeking a conveniently located property in one of Dublin’s most established residential areas. The development also benefits from ample parking for residents.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation comprises an entrance hall with useful storage leading through to an open-plan kitchen/living/dining room. This is a comfortable and bright main living space with room for both sitting and dining areas. A particular feature is the access to a private balcony overlooking Vernon Avenue, providing valuable outdoor space and allowing plenty of natural light into the room.\r\n\r\nThe kitchen is incorporated neatly within the living area and is fitted with a range of wall and floor units, worktop space, tiled splashback and integrated cooking appliances. Its open-plan arrangement works well for everyday living while keeping the overall space sociable and easy to maintain.\r\n\r\nThe bedroom is a comfortable double room with timber flooring and good natural light. Completing the accommodation is a shower room fitted with a glazed shower enclosure, WC and wash-hand basin.\r\n\r\nMerchamp is a mature and well-established development in an excellent Clontarf location. Vernon Avenue is only moments away and offers a good selection of everyday amenities, including shops, cafés, restaurants and local services. The wider Clontarf area provides an excellent choice of sporting and recreational facilities, while the seafront promenade is within easy reach for walking, running and cycling.\r\n\r\nThe location also offers convenient access to St Anne’s Park, Dollymount Strand and Bull Island, providing an excellent balance between city living and access to extensive green and coastal amenities.\r\n\r\nPublic transport connections are particularly convenient, with the 130 Dublin Bus route operating along Vernon Avenue, together with additional bus services and DART connections nearby. Dublin city centre, the IFSC and East Point Business Park are also readily accessible.\r\n\r\nApartment 34 Merchamp offers an attractive and manageable home in a settled Clontarf development, with the added benefits of a private balcony, ample resident parking and an excellent range of amenities close at hand."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Rooms",
